PY  - 2021
JO  - International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)
DO  - 10.48550/arXiv.2010.11929
UR  - https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.11929
AB  - While the Transformer architecture has become the de-facto standard for natural language processing tasks, its applications to computer vision remain limited. In vision, attention is either applied in conjunction with convolutional networks, or used to replace certain components of convolutional networks while keeping their overall structure in place. We show that this reliance on CNNs is not necessary and a pure transformer applied directly to sequences of image patches can perform very well on image classification tasks.
